    <p class="eyebrow">Kouvi Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: August 12, 2026</p>
    <p class="intro">Kouvi connects tennis enthusiasts through short training videos, livestreams, live video calls, tips, gear discussions, comments, and events. This policy explains the information needed to provide those experiences, how it is used, and the choices available to you.</p>
    <section><h2>1. Account and Profile Information</h2><p>We process information you provide when creating and personalizing an account, such as your email address, display name, profile photo, biography, tennis level, playing experience, interests, and selected preferences.</p></section>
    <section><h2>2. Posts and Community Activity</h2><p>We process the short videos, photos, captions, comments, likes, follows, gear discussions, event activity, reports, and other content you submit or interact with. Public posts and profile details may be visible to other Kouvi users.</p></section>
    <section><h2>3. Camera, Microphone, Photos, and Videos</h2><p>With your permission, camera and microphone access may be used to host livestreams, participate in live video calls, or create tennis content. Audio and video are transmitted to provide the live feature. Kouvi does not record a private video call unless a recording feature is clearly presented and the required consent is obtained.</p><p>When you use Apple’s system media picker, Kouvi receives only the photos or videos you explicitly select for a profile or post, rather than unrestricted access to your entire library.</p></section>
    <section><h2>4. Livestream and Video-Call Information</h2><p>Livestream content, chat, reactions, audience information, call participants, session timing, connection quality, and moderation signals may be processed to deliver real-time communication, manage hosts and viewers, improve call reliability, and respond to safety reports. Livestreams are intended for an audience and should be treated as public unless the app clearly indicates otherwise.</p></section>
    <section><h2>5. Usage, Device, and Safety Information</h2><p>We may process content interactions, followed accounts, event participation, app and device version, language, approximate timestamps, crash and performance data, network quality, and security records. If you submit a report, we process the report and relevant account or content information needed to review it.</p></section>
    <section><h2>6. How Information Is Used</h2><ul><li>provide accounts, profiles, posts, livestreams, video calls, comments, follows, and events;</li><li>transcode and deliver video and audio at suitable quality;</li><li>personalize tennis videos, creators, training topics, and event suggestions;</li><li>recommend content based on interests and activity;</li><li>detect spam, unsafe livestreams, harassment, fraud, and other rule violations;</li><li>investigate reports, enforce community standards, and protect users;</li><li>diagnose failures, improve performance, and develop Kouvi features;</li><li>respond to support requests and comply with legal obligations.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2>7. Public and Audience-Visible Information</h2><p>Your display name, profile photo, biography, tennis profile, posts, public livestreams, comments, likes, follows, and event activity may be visible to other users. A livestream host and other call participants can see and hear what your camera and microphone capture. Do not share information or surroundings you do not want your intended audience to receive.</p></section>
    <section><h2>8. Sharing of Information</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. Information may be shared with hosting, video-delivery, moderation, analytics, customer-support, and security providers that help operate Kouvi; with other users according to the feature you choose; with authorities when legally required; in a business transaction subject to appropriate safeguards; or when you direct or consent to sharing.</p></section>
    <section><h2>9. Retention and Security</h2><p>Account and content information is retained while needed to provide Kouvi. Reports, enforcement records, and limited copies of removed content may be retained for safety, dispute resolution, fraud prevention, and legal compliance. We use reasonable safeguards for stored and transmitted data, but no system can guarantee absolute security.</p></section>
    <section><h2>10. Your Controls and Rights</h2><p>You can choose what to post, whether to join a livestream or call, which accounts to follow, and whether to grant camera, microphone, and media permissions. Permissions can be changed in iOS Settings, although disabling one may prevent the related feature from working.</p><p>Depending on applicable law, you may request access to, correction of, export of, or deletion of your personal information and account through the support options in the app.</p></section>
    <section><h2>11. Children</h2><p>Kouvi is not intended for children below the minimum age required to consent to data processing in their location. We prohibit exploitation or inappropriate contact with minors. If we learn that information was collected from an ineligible child, we will take appropriate steps to delete it and restrict the relevant account.</p></section>
    <section><h2>12. International Processing</h2><p>Because tennis enthusiasts may connect across regions, information may be processed outside your place of residence where service infrastructure or providers operate, with safeguards required by applicable law.</p></section>
    <section><h2>13. Policy Updates</h2><p>We may revise this policy as Kouvi’s video, livestream, call, event, and community features evolve. Material changes will be communicated through the app when appropriate, and the updated date above will be revised.</p></section>
    <section><h2>14. Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, rights requests, or concerns about camera, microphone, livestream, or video-call data, contact the Kouvi support team through the support options in the app.</p></section>
